        {
          "path": "mcm_field_organism/_s2er_windows_files.py",
          "line": 169
        }
      ],
      "required": "Every fixture, recorder spool/staging, supervisor publication and reached native helper call must have an unambiguous preregistered path/role binding.",
      "actual": "The closed role set contains subject staging and final evidence targets, but no separate recorder staging/spool derivation or ancestor-directory role mapping. BoundPath provides only case_id, role and path.",
      "static_counterexamples": [
        "The p01 subject staging is renamed to the p01 result at E5. The separately published p01 trace needs a different fresh same-parent staging. Reusing role staging for a second path or adding trace_staging requires a rule absent from the closed contract.",
        "PlatformReport B, RecordingManifest and worker spools need distinct paths beyond the enumerated final targets; no closed derived-role relation identifies them.",
        "pin_parents opens path ancestors in addition to four ParentSet endpoints. read_source can open further source ancestors. Logging these as one of four endpoint roles is inaccurate; dropping their calls violates full-boundary recording."
      ],
      "impact": "All 13 case intents are present, but full E0 recording and recorder publication cannot be accepted as completely materializable without inventing a path-role rule.",
      "closure_requirements": [
        "Represent all needed recorder spools, publication stages, final targets and control evidence locations with unique artifact/case/actor binding.",
        "Bind all opened parent/source ancestors and their call roles deterministically to admitted paths without permitting arbitrary paths.",
        "Define uniqueness, collision rejection and the exact sentinel/p13 exceptions.",
        "Ensure every reached file/directory operation maps to exactly one preregistered identity; keep unknown paths fail-closed.",
        "Preserve cases, ordering, error provenance, completion rules, source isolation and all execution locks."
      ],
      "not_a_runtime_failure": true,
      "correction_performed": false
    }
  ],
